    "summary": "Somalia's opposition-led Somali Future Council has called on six African nations contributing to the AU mission to push for an inclusive political settlement alongside security support, amid unresolved tensions between the federal government and regional states.",
    "content": "The Somali Future Council, an opposition-led coalition, has written to the leaders of Uganda, Kenya, Ethiopia, Djibouti, Burundi, and Egypt urging them to prioritize an inclusive political agreement in Somalia alongside their security contributions. The letter, issued on July 27, highlights the need for a political settlement that addresses the ongoing tensions between the federal government and regional administrations such as Puntland and Jubaland.\n\nThese six countries provide troops and police to the African Union mission in Somalia, known as AUSSOM. The Council's appeal comes at a critical juncture for the country's security framework, as the AU mission continues to support Somali forces in combating insurgent groups.\n\nThe political rift between Mogadishu and regional states has persisted for months, complicating efforts to hold elections and implement constitutional reforms. The opposition argues that without a durable political deal, security gains remain fragile and the risk of renewed instability increases.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this issue is particularly significant because many families have roots in these regional states and closely follow governance and stability trends that affect investment, remittances, and return plans. A political resolution could pave the way for more coherent security and development strategies.\n\nThe letter's timing also coincides with ongoing debates in Somalia about the future of the AU mission and the country's ability to manage its own security. The opposition council's call suggests that external partners should leverage their influence to encourage dialogue between the federal government and regional leaders.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/07/27/opposition-council-urges-au-allies-to-push-political-deal/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=opposition-council-urges-au-allies-to-push-political-deal",
